    17	redefines the bug report reproduction process as a Markov model and finds the best paths through the model
    18	using a dynamic programming based technique. We conducted an empirical evaluation on 72 real-world bug
    19	reports. Our approach achieved a 94% reproduction rate on the total bug reports and a 93% reproduction rate
    20	on bug reports with missing steps, significantly outperforming the state-of-the-art approaches. Our approach
    21	was also more effective in finding the matches from the steps to UI events than the state-of-the-art approaches.
